<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45101" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spondēus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spondīus</span></b> ; sometimes incorrectly written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spondaeus</span></b> ), i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπονδεῖος</span>, of or
		belonging to libations; hence, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>substt.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spondēum</span></b> ,
			i, n., <i>a vessel used in
				making libations</i>, <i><span class="en">App. M. 11, p.
				266, 26</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> (Because of its prolonged, solemn character.) <i>A spondee</i> (metrical foot), <i><span class="en">Cic. Or.
				64, 216</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 9, 4, 80 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. A. P.
			256</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 21, 42</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
